industrial lasers, including short-pulse solid-state lasers and kilowatt-class fiber lasers. Its products and solutions are used in cloud, artificial intelligence and machine learning (AI/ML), telecommunications, consumer, and industrial end-market applications. The company was incorporated in 2015 and is headquartered in San Jose, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael E.  Hurlston | President, CEO & Director | Age 58 | Compensation: $3.1M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 13K people. Revenue per employee of $219K ranks in the bottom quartile among Technology peers, with revenue growing 12%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $22K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $12K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 14\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Lumentum Holdings Inc. is a large-cap technology business with a $41.8B market cap on $3.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +19% over the past three years and +13% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 13% against a 12% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, with gross margins sitting at 32%.","The business throws off $300M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 10 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 24\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 405% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and